# Build context of the engine image (Dockerfile at the repo root).
# Allow-list: send only what the image needs. Everything else -- .git, secrets/, .env files,
# the console, demo, evals, caches -- never reaches the Docker daemon.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!prompts/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
**/.env*
**/secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
